  "update_check": "Publisher, PMID 24769869, and Crossref work record showed no linked correction in the inspection; Crossref relation {}. The preprint's Fig. 4 explanatory paragraph shows a real sign where the published version gives -i. Fig. 4 describes theory. The measured configurations in Figs. 2,3,5,6 use the antisymmetric circular input. A real-input experiment was not identified in this paper."
 },
 "apparatus": "Source localized at site 0, circular (H-iV)/sqrt(2) in H/V order. Eq. (1) coin C(theta)=[[cos2theta,sin2theta],[sin2theta,-cos2theta]]. At the defect n multiply both outgoing amplitudes by exp(+i phi) on departure, H goes left and V right. Eq. (2)'s two explicitly stated basis actions and the polarization-independent phase plate specify this convention. Its symbol S-dagger is not literally the inverse of the stated left shift.",
 "alternative": "At each physical site split its actual incoming probability between coin outputs in proportion to their complex modulus to the fourth power, then stream; zero-total cells carry zero mass. Born uses the same coherent amplitudes. Sum both outgoing coin weights at a final site. For nonbalanced HWP settings this explicitly extends the tested rule. Equal initial circular moduli give initial weights 1/2,1/2.",
 "measurement": "Site coincidence counts divided by total detected counts at the respective step. 7 ns coincidence window, roughly 300 coincidences/s collected over 60 s as an apparatus statement, visibility 0.998 per interferometer pair. No absolute detection probabilities, per-bin raw counts or covariance matrix were obtained. Common attenuation cancels; unequal efficiencies, dephasing, state errors and drift need independent calibration.",
